    "history": "Section 6.4 of docs/archive/plan-npc.md, registered 2026-10-26 before any measured game: chess on 8 by 9 won by taking the king, stalemate a loss, a duck that starts on e5 and walks a king's step, and four wild pieces that eat nothing, touch the four squares beside them and pace their lines (a gorgon freezing on a5-c5 and a siren disarming on h5-f5, alone on the middle rank; dryads shielding on c4-f4 and c6-f6), turning back at a block and returning eight phases after they are taken. Built on the menagerie's lesson (its stalemate draws and smothering effects); registered as drafted after a draft read in self-play at 1600 and 6400 nodes.",
